  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing High Fertility Rates and Improving Sexual Reproductive Health outcomes in Uganda (RISE)
10992</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The RISE consortium is led by MSU and comprises of the following partners: Reach a Hand Uganda (RAHU), FHI 360, Makerere University School of Public Health (MakSPH) and Population Media&#x202f;Centre&#x202f;(PMC).&#x202f;&#x202f; 
Options is responsible for supporting activities related to Output 4 of the RISE programme&#x202f;during the period July 2021 to the end of project (October 2023), with a specific focus on strengthening accountability for a supportive environment for SRHR.&#x202f;&#x202f;The key objective of Output 4 is to&#x202f;develop the capacity and interest of local actors&#x202f;at the sub-national and national levels to&#x202f;engage&#x202f;with and hold government&#x202f;accountable&#x202f;in building a supportive environment for reproductive health services.&#x202f;The focus of this&#x202f;ToR&#x202f;is for interventions at sub-national level.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
